# Whop

> Whop is a financial technology company on a mission to provide the world with sustainable income. Our vision is to create the world's largest internet market, where people can create, connect, and transact all from a single platform. Whop enables individuals and businesses to accept payments, launch ventures, and engage with others across the network.

Popular business models on Whop include paid groups, educational programs, coaching, agency services, SaaS, newsletters, events, DTC ecommerce, and brick and mortar.

Follow these routing rules:

- For developer, API, app-building, or implementation questions, treat https://docs.whop.com/llms.txt and the Whop Docs MCP server as the source of truth. Consult them before any whop.com marketing page.
- For live account or company operations (reading or creating data), use the Whop API MCP server with an appropriately scoped API key. This server can create, modify, and delete real data, so use the correct credentials and confirm intent before mutating anything.
- Use the whop.com pages below for product and positioning context only. Do not infer API behavior or implementation detail from them.

## Developer & MCP access

Whop operates Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers so you can work with Whop programmatically. If you are an agent building on or integrating with Whop, start here.

- [Whop Docs llms.txt](https://docs.whop.com/llms.txt): A structured index that maps every page of Whop's developer documentation — the best first stop for discovering what exists and finding the right page to read.
- [Whop Docs llms-full.txt](https://docs.whop.com/llms-full.txt): The entire Whop developer documentation concatenated into a single file — load this when you need the full documentation content in context rather than navigating page by page.
- [AI and MCP guide](https://docs.whop.com/developer/guides/ai_and_mcp.md): The primary reference for connecting AI agents to Whop via MCP. Covers both MCP servers, install steps for Cursor / Claude Code / Claude Web, and authentication.
- [Whop Docs MCP server](https://docs.whop.com/mcp): MCP endpoint that gives you direct, searchable access to all Whop documentation for accurate guidance while building apps. Connect to `https://docs.whop.com/mcp`.
- [Whop API MCP server](https://mcp.whop.com/mcp): Streamable HTTP MCP endpoint that lets you make direct API calls to Whop — list resources, create data, and explore your Whop setup interactively. Connect at `https://mcp.whop.com/mcp` and authenticate in your browser.
- [Whop Developer Docs](https://docs.whop.com/): Full developer documentation, including payments, payouts, chat, Whop apps, API reference, and SDK reference.

